**MSVC rejects `this` in a nested lambda's init-capture.** Found 2026-09-07 at
commit fbe5963b: `CallAfter([self=wxWeakRef<wxWindow>(this),...])` written INSIDE
another lambda compiled on clang but failed on MSVC with 37 errors, because MSVC
bound that `this` to the enclosing closure object, so it tried to build a
`wxWeakRef<wxWindow>` from a lambda pointer
(`Tracked_class_should_inherit_from_wxTrackable`). Name the object first —
`auto* menu = this;` then capture `menu`. Watch for this pattern whenever a
deferred callback is set up from within another lambda; it is invisible on macOS.
EOF
echo "memory updated"
cat > /Users/kenneth/jusprin-win-vm-harness/msvc-nested-lambda-this.patch <<'EOF'
Verified on the Windows VM: without this, commit fbe5963b fails to compile with
37 MSVC errors. With it, the build is clean (exit 0) and both chip menus open
without crashing.

--- a/src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Shell/HeaderControls.cpp
+++ b/src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Shell/HeaderControls.cpp
@@ HeaderMenu::build, wxEVT_MENU handler
             button->Bind(wxEVT_MENU,[this,action=std::move(item.invoke_row_action)](wxCommandEvent&) {
                 // Like keeps_open rows, this rebuilds the popup's own contents.
-                CallAfter([self=wxWeakRef<wxWindow>(this),action] { if (self) action(); });
+                // MSVC binds `this` in a nested lambda's init-capture to the
+                // enclosing closure, not the class, so name the menu first.
+                auto* menu = this;
+                CallAfter([self=wxWeakRef<wxWindow>(menu),action] { if (self) action(); });
             });
@@ HeaderMenu::build, wxEVT_BUTTON handler
             if (keeps_open) {
                 // The handler rebuilds this menu's rows, which destroys the
                 // button currently delivering this event. Defer past it.
-                CallAfter([self=wxWeakRef<wxWindow>(this),invoke] { if (self) invoke(); });
+                auto* menu = this;
+                CallAfter([self=wxWeakRef<wxWindow>(menu),invoke] { if (self) invoke(); });
                 return;
             }
EOF
