Name the menu before capturing it in a nested lambda

MSVC binds this in a nested lambda init-capture to the enclosing closure
rather than the enclosing class, so wxWeakRef<wxWindow>(this) inside
HeaderMenu::build tried to wrap a lambda pointer and failed with
Tracked_class_should_inherit_from_wxTrackable. Clang resolves it to
HeaderMenu, so this only broke the Windows build.

Verified on a Windows VM: the branch failed with 37 MSVC errors before this
change and builds clean after, with both header chip menus opening and their
sublists working without crashing.

